 7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\n*** COSTUME / HAIR / MAKEUP — Clara ***\nClara —
  Costume (you provide): Pink Seamless Tights\, Flesh-tone camisole leota
 rd\; Shoes: Pink Ballet Shoes\; Makeup: Light/Medium Stage Makeup\; Hair
 : Half Up-Half Down\, Curls (natural or curled)\; Accessories (BA provid
 es): 2 Hair Bows\; Prop (BA provides): Nutcracker\nLight Stage Makeup In
 struction Sheet:\n• Powder matching skintone\n• Light brown eye shad
 ow applied to the crease with an eye shadow brush\n• Dark Brown/Black 
 eyeliner and black mascara. No fake lashes.\n• Blush on the cheeks (be
  sure to apply plenty so dancer doesn’t look washed out in the stage l
 ights)\n• Red or Dark Red lipstick\nDancers of Color may wear flesh to
 ne tights and flesh tone ballet shoes.\nCostume Care Guidelines:\n• Ha
 ndle costume pieces with care while changing to prevent damage to delica
 te fabrics\n• Promptly notify Ballet Arkansas in the event of costume 
 damage at the point of discovery\, no matter how significant\n• Never 
 throw costumes or accessories on the floor\, or hang costumes by their e
 lastic straps\n• Refrain from sitting on the floor while in costume\n
 • Do not attempt to alter\, mend\, clean\, or launder any costume or a
 ccessory\n• Never apply stage make-up while in costume and shall take 
 great care to refrain from smudging make-up on costume during its remova
 l\n• Refrain from the use of spray perfume or cologne while in costume
 \n• Never wear any garment not assigned to cast member\n• Do not han
 dle or consume food or beverage while in costume\, with the exception of
  water\n• Do not remove costumes from their assigned dressing rooms or
  from the theater\n• Remove all bobby pins used to secure head pieces 
 and wigs following their use\n• Return all headpieces to their assigne
 d bags\n• Comply fully with any and all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ 
 wardrobe policies\n• Do not pack markers\, paints\, colored drinks or 
 anything that may damage or stain costumes.
